+def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
+    """
+    Rebuild the missing D4-symmetric ground patch, then let the isolated tokens settle downward onto the restored terrain.
+
+    Input structure:
+    - The input is a square grid whose intended terrain pattern is D4-symmetric under horizontal, vertical, and diagonal reflections.
+    - One all-black rectangular patch has been erased from that terrain, and the erased cells can be recovered from their symmetry orbits.
+    - Several isolated single-pixel tokens use colors outside the terrain palette and sit in the upper half on otherwise empty cells.
